UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Page of Swords represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Observation"—the high-alert, investigative phase where the sovereign consciousness, having survived the hard-crash of the Ten, begins to process its environment with the objective, questioning, and slightly detached curiosity of a student of reality. Moving beyond the terminal cycle of the Ten, the Page signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Scout," where you are not yet the master strategist, but you are becoming the highly effective gatherer of data, intelligence, and nuance. Visually depicted as a young figure standing alert with a sword held aloft against a windswept, cloudy sky, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Vigilance"—the realization that true insight requires an active, curious, and questioning engagement with the world. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Systemic Scanning," where you are initiating your new operating system by cataloging the terrain, identifying potential logical hazards, and learning to navigate the world through objective deduction rather than emotional reactivity. When the Page of Swords appears, your system is registering a "High-Sensitivity" status; you are at the beginning of a new mental development, and you are being invited to stop the "victim-narrative" of your past and instead perform a brutal, surgical audit of your present-day input. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your intellectual discipline. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Inquisitiveness": questioning the baseline assumptions of your environment, identifying the gaps in your knowledge, and learning to communicate your findings with clarity, precision, and zero egoic attachment. To inhabit the Page of Swords is to master the art of "Strategic Observation," recognizing that by choosing to see the world as a complex data-set waiting to be understood, you are effectively laying the groundwork for a massive, structural increase in your own, sovereign intelligence.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Page of Swords appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Paranoia," "Information-Fragmentation," or the catastrophic—yet curative—failure to integrate the data you are gathering, leading to a state of superficial, scattered, and often defensive reactivity. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "being constantly on guard" with "being smart," even as you realize your internal operating system is experiencing a critical, logic-based failure of its "relevance-filtering" protocol. You are essentially "processing noise as signal," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "look informed" or "be one step ahead" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually understand what is happening. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "sharp-witted detective," while internally, you are being jolted by a profound, gnawing sense of intellectual chaos, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of "jumping to conclusions," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your "sharpness" is a brittle, defensive mask. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of information-overload"; you are obsessively trying to stay ahead of perceived threats, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final stabilization of your intellect is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to drop the "vigilant" act and sit quietly with the unknown, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. The reversed Page of Swords exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "being caught unaware," and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense of the "intellectual skeptic" and face the truth of your own, present-day, unintegrated self, you would be forced to acknowledge that your "sharpness" was a defensive response to your own, underlying sense of helplessness. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these frantic, data-gathering, worry-looping scripts, perform a brutal audit of your intellectual discipline, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize the integrity of your discernment over the convenience of your defensive posturing. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical cognitive-grounding—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "the illusion of control" over the vulnerability of "the reality of observation," and realizing that until you are willing to slow down, verify your data, and act with the patient, unadorned truth of a master student, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom intellectual superiority you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 39;
